  <activityDataset>
    <activityDescription>
      <activity id="45c926ca-4ba3-5f3f-9a5f-ecc465cd9261" activityNameId="08933c4b-33e3-561e-aeab-fcde0b5b34e5" activityNameContextId="f44c43c1-5cc5-54a6-ade6-24435bd12c83" type="1" specialActivityType="0" energyValues="0">
        <activityName xml:lang="en">Hot rolling, steel</activityName>
        <generalComment>
          <text xml:lang="en" index="1">Full activity name: Hot rolling, steel
To achieve greater toughness, shock resistance and tensile strength, the raw steel production outputs cast ingots, slabs, billets and beam blanks are hot rolled to long or flat products or semifinished products.;
Synonyms: Hot forming; 
UUID: 79cdf328-b4c5-3885-a6ed-fcf7b5c0afcd
Includes the process steps scarfing, grinding heating, descaling, rolling and finishing. Semiclosed water circuit with water treatment plant is also included. Does not include the material being rolled
Location: Data-set is representative for European Union
Technology: Average technique for EU. Assumption: heating 100% with natural gas. Furnaces of about 10 MW are approxi-mated by furnace "&gt; 100 kW"
Time period: undefined
Production volume: 127.8 million tonnes in 1996
Sampling: Literature 
Extrapolations: none
Uncertainty adjustments: The fact that no data were available about the percentage of companies represented by the study citated is considered in the uncertainties.
BAFU mapped export: unsupported biosphere exchanges excluded; see audit/. Local UUIDs and generic activity classification are export conventions. Source: process_79cdf328-b4c5-3885-a6ed-fcf7b5c0afcd.xml</text>
        </generalComment>
      </activity>
